Processing of our usersâ queries
To respond to the query by displaying results and ads matching your search, as well as for security and reliability purposes of its services (detection of spam, automated activity, fraudulent clicks on adsâ¦), Qwant processes the following data:
â The entered keywords;
â Information about the browser you use (the User Agent);
â Session preferences information (if you use Qwant set up for the results in France and with the user interface in the French language, for example);
â A salted hash of the userâs IP address with the salt that changes ever three months at the latest (i.e.
the result of a mathematical formula based on this IP address, not the IP address itself);
â The approximate geographic area of origin of the search at the scale of a region or a city (as deduced from the IP address)
Qwant retains for 7 days the keyword(s) entered associated with a pseudonym identifier calculated from the User Agent of your browser and the salted hash of your IP address.

For this purpose, as well as for the security and reliability of our partnerâs services (detection of spam, automated activity, fraudulent clicks on adsâ¦), Qwant may transfer to this partner the following pseudonymous data related to your query:
â The searched keywords;
â The type and version of the browser used (User Agent);
â The first three bytes of your IP address;
â The approximate geographical area at the origin of the search, at the scale of a region or a city;
â A salted hash generated from: your IP address, your User Agent and a salt that changes at least every 3 months.

Statistics and audience measurement
To evaluate its audience and understand the use of its services in order to improve them, Qwant also keeps other data related to your use of the services (associated for 7 days with a hash calculated from your IP address and the User Agent of your browser) including :
â The source of the userâs visit to the site (the HTTP referrer and the search field used to trigger the request);
â Information about the type of link clicked (for example the position of the clicked link in the results with the number of results proposed);
â Some information deduced from your User Agent (type of browser, operating system, major version of the browser,â¦)
This processing is necessary for the purposes of Qwantâs legitimate interest in developing statistics and measuring its audience, based on article 6.1.f of the GDPR.

